 an id attribute that specifies an id reference.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"barStyle","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The style and color of the barline.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"footnote","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The footnote element specifies editorial information that appears in footnotes in the printed score. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"level","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The level element specifies editorial information for different MusicXML elements. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"wavyLine","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A wavy line associated with the barline, such as for a trill or vibrato that continues across it.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"segno","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The visual indicator of a segno sign appearing at this barline.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"coda","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The visual indicator of a coda sign appearing at this barline.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"fermata","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The fermata signs on either side of the barline, allowing fermatas on both sides (the lower one inverted).","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"ending","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The multiple-ending bracket associated with this barline.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"repeat","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The repeat mark associated with this barline.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"location","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"code":"right","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"segnoAttribute","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Used the same way as the segno attribute of the sound element, to name and distinguish forward jumps to a segno sign for playback.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"codaAttribute","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Used the same way as the coda attribute of the sound element, to name and distinguish forward jumps to a coda sign for playback.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"divisions","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Used the same way as the divisions attribute of the sound element, to indicate the number of divisions per quarter note for playback when this barline contains a segno or coda child element.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"code":"MXLBarline","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/init(id:barStyle:footnote:level:wavyLine:segno:coda:fermata:ending:repeat:location:segnoAttribute:codaAttribute:divisions:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Initializer","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"barStyle"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLBarlineV10StyleColorV","text":"StyleColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"footnote"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLFormattedTextV","text":"MXLFormattedText"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"level"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","text":"MXLLevel"},{"